Structure version of the bundled dppdp9_epo2.xsd, and the row číselník of the
výkazy filed inside it, pinned by hand.

WHY A FILE AND NOT A FIELD IN THE SCHEMA: there isn't one. `verzePis` is a
bare xs:string with no fixed value, and the XSD carries no version stamp of its
own; the Finanční správa overwrites the one file in place (one XSD for every
zdaňovací období it accepts — currently 2021-2025 and parts of 2026). A stale
copy validates exactly as cleanly as a current one. This file is the only
thing that makes a refresh visible; tests/test_cz_dppo.py checks the digests
and the template's `verzePis` against it.

THE ČÍSELNÍK IS NOT IN THE XSD. VetaUA / VetaUB / VetaUD carry `c_radku` as a
3-digit decimal and nothing else; which numbers exist, what they designate and
which rozsah (P / Z / M) they belong to is an EPO application číselník,
published only as HTML. data/uv_radky_500.csv is that číselník for vyhláška
500/2002 Sb. (tables A = VetaUA, P = VetaUD, D = VetaUB), extracted from
  https://adisspr.mfcr.cz/dpr/adis/idpr_pub/hlib/uv_info/info_detail.faces?tabulka=23810&platnost=2025
  https://adisspr.mfcr.cz/dpr/adis/idpr_pub/hlib/uv_info/info_detail.faces?tabulka=24810&platnost=2025
  https://adisspr.mfcr.cz/dpr/adis/idpr_pub/hlib/uv_info/info_detail.faces?tabulka=25810&platnost=2025
(index: .../hlib/uv_info/uv_info.faces?rok=2025). Platnost 2024, 2025 and 2026
are identical row for row, verified 2026-09-28.

REFRESH PROCEDURE
  1. Fetch  https://adisspr.mfcr.cz/adis/jepo/schema/dppdp9_epo2.xsd  (plain
     curl). A miss is HTTP 200 with ZERO bytes — test the size, not the code.
  2. Compare against data/dppdp9_epo2.xsd byte for byte.
  3. Read Verze / Ze dne from
     https://adisspr.mfcr.cz/dpr/adis/idpr_pub/epo2_info/popis_struktury_detail.faces?zkratka=DPPDP9
  4. Re-extract the three číselník tables for the new platnost and diff them
     against data/uv_radky_500.csv.
  5. If anything moved: replace the files, update the lines at the top of this
     file, the `verzePis` literal in report/dppo_report.xml, and the mapping in
     models/dppdp9_vykazy.py. Nothing keeps them in step automatically; the
     tests only make the drift loud.

